  "explanation_result": {
    "decision": "EXPLAINED",
    "explanation": "The +6.7% day\u2011over\u2011day jump on 2021\u201107\u201120 was driven by fresh news of worsening supply conditions in Brazil. Multiple reports published on the same day highlighted a sudden frost that hit Brazilian coffee\u2011growing regions, raising fears of further crop loss (source: 39a26aa0fd5c7937; 75fbfa71adcdb235; 79f3bda60f07ae5a). These frost reports were combined with ongoing drought impacts and higher shipping costs noted in a same\u2011day story about supply\u2011chain disruptions and a USDA\u2011reported 19% drop in Brazil\u2019s coffee production (source: 3c767b8ecb0f788b). The convergence of immediate weather\u2011related damage and existing drought\u2011driven shortages created a clear supply\u2011concern narrative that explains the sharp price increase.",
